1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,680
This ice was frozen by the night sky.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,240
In the deserts of Persia,

3
00:00:04,310 --> 00:00:06,510
winter nights hover around freezing.

4
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,630
So builders dug long, shallow pools,

5
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,220
fed by underground canals,

6
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:13,490
and raised a tall mud brick wall

7
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:14,670
along the south side.

8
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,810
By day, the wall threw shade over the water.

9
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:19,960
By night, the water lost its heat

10
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:22,630
straight up into the clear, dry sky,

11
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:24,650
and a thin skin of ice formed,

12
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,630
even when the air was likely a little above freezing.

13
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:29,760
Each night workers poured on

14
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:31,330
a few more inches of water.

15
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:32,550
Layer by layer,

16
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,020
the ice grew to about twenty inches thick.

17
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,750
Then they cut it into blocks

18
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,720
and carried it into a domed pit,

19
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:39,880
packed with straw.

20
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,990
Some of these domes stand almost sixty feet tall.

21
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:46,520
In midsummer, whole towns drank iced sherbet,

22
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,290
all thanks to the night sky.
